WEBVTT

00:05.120 --> 00:06.650
Sorry I'm late!

00:06.650 --> 00:08.900
I ran into a spot of trouble.

00:08.900 --> 00:13.860
Now, what sort of "fire" 
do you have to show me?

00:13.860 --> 00:19.610
My friends tell me I'm something 
of a "summer bug," you see.

00:21.040 --> 00:25.910
I'd appreciate a beautiful flame. 
One worth flying into.

01:57.570 --> 01:59.470
<b></b>Rental Garage

01:57.980 --> 01:59.470
What is it?

01:59.470 --> 02:00.830
Jackpot.

02:00.830 --> 02:02.930
That's Hosorogi-san for you.

02:03.240 --> 02:08.390
Documentation on that fire 100 years ago, 
in the building we visited yesterday.

02:12.610 --> 02:13.990
Who might you be?

02:13.990 --> 02:14.690
Huh?!

02:14.690 --> 02:16.750
O-Oh, excuse us.

02:16.750 --> 02:18.650
Er... No need to worry.

02:18.920 --> 02:20.510
We're with the police.

02:21.600 --> 02:25.580
We're questioning people in relation 
to a Public Safety investigation.

02:26.530 --> 02:32.370
That man claimed he manages the house 
at the owner's request, but I wonder.

02:32.370 --> 02:38.520
The owner confirmed his story, 
and his identity checked out.

02:38.910 --> 02:39.720
Right.

02:40.230 --> 02:43.230
So we couldn't dig deeper then,

02:43.230 --> 02:45.930
but with these documents
I think we have a shot.

02:46.530 --> 02:48.390
Thanks, Hosorogi-san.

02:49.020 --> 02:53.930
I promise you I'll reach the 
darkness called "Sabaramond"!

02:57.320 --> 03:00.740
By the way, Clarissa, 
what are our plans for tomorrow?

03:00.740 --> 03:02.540
We'll spectate this time.

03:03.060 --> 03:04.070
Are you sure?

03:04.330 --> 03:07.600
I'd like to gauge how far he'll go.

03:08.220 --> 03:11.540
Though, naturally, I'll keep 
my word as an intermediary.

03:13.190 --> 03:17.210
Even spectating requires
 some preparation.

03:18.470 --> 03:20.970
What has that trio been up to?

03:21.260 --> 03:26.930
Nothing since yesterday, when they 
met a man we believe to be Solitaire.

03:27.370 --> 03:29.890
Are they at odds with Solitaire?

03:29.890 --> 03:33.830
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

03:31.250 --> 03:33.850
Who are these people holding umbrellas?

03:34.400 --> 03:35.300
"Fire."

03:36.220 --> 03:37.780
Solitaire.

03:40.030 --> 03:42.550
Could they be... the Fire-Breathing Bug?

03:43.940 --> 03:46.240
It's almost the time we agreed on.

03:46.530 --> 03:48.970
That guy Taipei is gonna show, right?

03:48.970 --> 03:53.960
To be honest, I don't know exactly 
who or what those three are.

03:54.310 --> 04:00.950
But if Takeru-san sees them as a threat to 
the Shinoyamas, he may choose to send aid.

04:01.290 --> 04:04.050
What about after we rescue Polka-kun?

04:04.420 --> 04:08.260
I think I can hold off the 
elemental. And then...

04:08.260 --> 04:10.950
Me and Xiaoyu-kun get our time to shine!

04:11.540 --> 04:14.060
I've gotten the hang of my right arm.

04:14.060 --> 04:16.690
Training with those tigers helped.

04:16.690 --> 04:17.860
Hey, listen up!

04:17.860 --> 04:21.340
Even in shark movies, 
nameless characters die first.

04:21.340 --> 04:22.460
Where'd that come from?!

04:22.780 --> 04:26.570
My point is, what should we 
call you versus the real Polka?

04:26.570 --> 04:29.940
Good point. We might get 
confused when it counts.

04:29.940 --> 04:32.450
We only know you as "the Corpse God."

04:32.780 --> 04:35.580
You said your real name's hard 
to say in Japanese, right?

04:37.420 --> 04:38.740
Polka-kun?

04:38.740 --> 04:40.800
Sorry. I lied.

04:41.770 --> 04:45.690
It is a bit tricky to say, 
but hardly unpronounceable.

04:46.350 --> 04:50.350
I just didn't want to tell you because 
it brings back unpleasant memories.

04:50.810 --> 04:54.100
But this is a good chance, 
so I'll tell you now.

04:54.420 --> 04:55.850
My real name is—

04:57.220 --> 04:57.860
Wait.

04:58.150 --> 05:00.930
The real Polka-kun's 
location started to move.

05:05.340 --> 05:08.130
The two women just left the hotel.

05:08.130 --> 05:09.850
Two of the three?

05:12.140 --> 05:14.120
What happened to the other one?

05:17.170 --> 05:18.040
Huh?

05:18.260 --> 05:19.420
What's up?

05:21.720 --> 05:24.420
Hi. As promised, I'm here to see you.

05:26.720 --> 05:28.640
This time, as a friend.

05:28.920 --> 05:32.100
What'd this guy bother to show up for?

05:32.570 --> 05:36.560
Hey, wait! I'd know if you used the entrance!

05:36.560 --> 05:39.900
Oh, I took the liberty of using 
your underground passage.

05:41.340 --> 05:43.360
Don't be so nervous.

05:43.970 --> 05:46.910
I only came to befriend you.

05:47.330 --> 05:49.490
To... befriend?

05:49.800 --> 05:50.920
Yes.

05:50.920 --> 05:55.190
Precious few people in this world 
are capable of understanding me.

05:55.190 --> 05:56.680
The same goes for you,

05:56.680 --> 06:00.420
or should I say, "your power"?

06:01.140 --> 06:04.170
<i>Does he realize I come from the other world?</i>

06:04.590 --> 06:08.780
You must have lived in such confusion. 
I feel for you.

06:08.780 --> 06:12.900
But you shouldn't shun your power. 
You should take pride in it.

06:13.550 --> 06:18.600
The power you inherited from your mother 
comes from the same world as mine.

06:19.750 --> 06:21.060
What are you talking about?

06:21.280 --> 06:24.160
Your mother, Kanon Shinoyama.

06:24.160 --> 06:27.780
Or rather, a descendant of a 
clan with the Elemental Eye,

06:28.050 --> 06:30.580
Kanomshelin Redrazalf.

06:34.190 --> 06:37.080
<i>What did he just say?</i>

06:37.380 --> 06:39.540
Polka-kun? What's wrong?

06:39.540 --> 06:44.460
<i>I always wondered why I 
reincarnated into this body.</i>

06:45.140 --> 06:49.060
<i>I should have delved deeper into 
Polka-kun's memories before now.</i>

06:50.290 --> 06:53.590
<i>This faint memory in his deepest depths...</i>

06:54.250 --> 06:57.110
<i>This feeling so distant 
it threatens to vanish...</i>

07:01.370 --> 07:06.370
<i>It's the name of someone 
I ultimately failed to save.</i>

07:07.240 --> 07:11.220
<i>I never thought I'd hear it in this world.</i>

07:11.850 --> 07:15.410
<i>I wonder if she found a 
peaceful life in the end.</i>

07:15.910 --> 07:17.050
<i>Mom.</i>

07:19.100 --> 07:23.450
<i>I placed one condition on 
my reincarnation spell:</i>

07:23.960 --> 07:29.020
<i>that I would possess the newly deceased 
body of a member of my people.</i>

07:29.610 --> 07:33.870
<i>I never dreamed it would link me to Mom,
 or that she'd come to this world.</i>

07:34.190 --> 07:35.290
Polka-kun?

07:36.570 --> 07:37.560
<i>Polka-kun,</i>

07:38.320 --> 07:40.510
<i>could you "see," too?</i>

07:40.510 --> 07:45.120
<i>Mom might have taught you so many things.</i>

07:52.950 --> 07:56.810
<i>Oh, we have so much to talk about.</i>

07:58.660 --> 08:02.170
I need to speak with you again, face-to-face.

08:04.540 --> 08:08.500
So I'll need you to return Polka-kun.

08:08.500 --> 08:11.630
My friend. My little brother!

08:13.470 --> 08:15.950
<i>Return who? His brother?</i>

08:16.410 --> 08:19.120
<i>Have I gotten something very wrong?</i>

08:19.690 --> 08:23.100
<i>He looks like Polka Shinoyama, 
but is he someone else on the inside?</i>

08:23.100 --> 08:27.060
<i>Then his rightful contents, his soul is...</i>

08:29.510 --> 08:31.530
<i>in that shark?</i>

08:34.360 --> 08:37.570
<i>Well, never mind. I haven't 
gotten to my real point yet.</i>

08:38.240 --> 08:42.200
If you come from the other side 
of the sky, the other world,

08:42.200 --> 08:45.040
and you have ties to this emblem,

08:45.490 --> 08:47.880
then you're involved with the Empire.

08:48.250 --> 08:53.120
How would you like to join forces 
and exterminate our enemy, the Bug?

08:53.580 --> 08:55.050
The Fire-Breathing Bug?

08:55.050 --> 08:58.890
Yes. I'm glad you don't beat around the bush.

08:58.890 --> 09:01.010
I have one question.

09:01.450 --> 09:07.100
Do you know Sabaramond-san? 
I mean, Arius-san?

09:07.450 --> 09:09.350
Well, there's a surprise!

09:09.350 --> 09:11.440
Are you personally acquainted, by any chance?

09:11.650 --> 09:13.400
You haven't answered me.

09:15.110 --> 09:19.050
I know <i>of</i> him, but we've never met.

09:19.360 --> 09:23.130
I'm something like his bastard child.

09:24.270 --> 09:28.580
Two of the three seem to be 
making for Polka's building.

09:29.010 --> 09:33.030
Do as you please. The woman 
you fought is one of them.

09:33.030 --> 09:34.050
Yes, sir.

09:34.260 --> 09:35.970
I'll ask you straight.

09:35.970 --> 09:38.010
Would you join our organization?

09:38.220 --> 09:39.970
No, thank you.

09:39.970 --> 09:41.390
No hesitation.

09:41.390 --> 09:44.230
I want a peaceful life.

09:44.640 --> 09:47.190
I don't know what your goal is,

09:47.190 --> 09:49.920
but I can't tolerate your methods.

09:49.920 --> 09:52.900
I'd <i>much</i> rather work with 
the Phantom Solitaire.

09:52.900 --> 09:56.310
Oh, you mean what Habaki got up to?

09:56.310 --> 09:59.670
He did all that on his 
own initiative, you know?

09:59.670 --> 10:02.910
Arius-san never tried to dodge 
his responsibility as a superior.

10:04.680 --> 10:08.250
So you <i>do</i> know Arius well.

10:08.570 --> 10:10.770
I've never met him,

10:11.080 --> 10:15.460
but being compared to him and found 
wanting kind of rubs me the wrong way,

10:16.190 --> 10:19.960
since he basically birthed me into 
this world and then abandoned me.

10:22.140 --> 10:23.220
He abandoned you?

10:23.220 --> 10:25.800
I'd say none of us is in 
the mood to chat anymore,

10:26.440 --> 10:30.410
so I'd like you to show me your power.

10:30.410 --> 10:34.720
Especially if you're something 
other than Polka Shinoyama.

10:34.720 --> 10:37.700
All right. I'm glad you like to talk so much.

10:40.490 --> 10:43.410
I had all the time in the 
world to cast my spells.

10:45.360 --> 10:46.950
Whoa!

10:47.760 --> 10:49.370
Wh-What the—?!

10:49.960 --> 10:50.540
<i>Bones?!</i>

10:51.290 --> 10:55.620
<i>I'm sure of it! This is no 
elementalism or general sorcery!</i>

10:55.620 --> 10:59.130
<i>If my information on the other 
world is correct, then this is</i>

10:59.560 --> 11:00.960
<i>necromancy!</i>

11:01.730 --> 11:02.590
<i>Could he be...</i>

11:02.950 --> 11:04.670
<i>Izliz Swordflail?!</i>

11:05.190 --> 11:06.310
<i>No, not her!</i>

11:06.970 --> 11:11.050
<i>Arius had close ties to 
three powerful necromancers!</i>

11:11.570 --> 11:15.590
<i>And the one his attitude and 
words so far point to is...</i>

11:16.730 --> 11:19.490
Are you... ranked fourth?

11:21.540 --> 11:26.240
Are you a leader of the imperial 
court sorcerers, the Corpse God?!

11:27.540 --> 11:29.120
I'm getting chills, and I don't know why.

11:29.120 --> 11:34.380
Maybe excitement? I've got a hunch 
that I'm caught up in something huge.

11:34.820 --> 11:37.950
But that just means I'm close to a big scoop!

11:37.950 --> 11:40.380
Go for it, Kochou! Get that story!

11:40.680 --> 11:43.390
Let's go!

11:46.000 --> 11:48.140
So, it's begun.

11:48.140 --> 11:51.600
<b><i>Fire
Safety</i></b>

11:48.540 --> 11:51.130
We settle things here.

11:52.410 --> 11:56.940
Implant our will in that child.

11:57.370 --> 12:01.140
Do that, and we will reach

11:57.960 --> 12:01.550
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

12:01.740 --> 12:04.950
the nest of bugs we must burn.

12:05.870 --> 12:07.200
Hey there.

12:07.200 --> 12:10.700
Mind answering a few questions 
for me, on the record,

12:11.280 --> 12:13.010
Fire-Breathing Bug-san?

12:14.560 --> 12:19.500
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

12:15.770 --> 12:19.500
Where are you all going with those 
umbrellas on such a nice day?

12:19.750 --> 12:21.720
Why, hello there, detectives.

12:22.490 --> 12:23.890
Thank you for the other day.

12:26.430 --> 12:31.340
Anyway, what do you need? 
You turned up so suddenly.

12:31.340 --> 12:35.310
And "Fire-Breathing Bug"? Isn't that 
the name of an infamous arsonist?

12:35.730 --> 12:36.460
Yeah.

12:36.890 --> 12:40.170
But "the Fire-Breathing Bug" 
isn't the name of an individual.

12:40.550 --> 12:46.360
And by the time that name spread,
 the people it really belonged to were gone.

12:46.710 --> 12:50.170
Someone left me papers that laid it all out.

12:50.610 --> 12:54.830
About the human experiments 
done in this house.

12:55.140 --> 12:58.040
Mitsu Haigawara and Takejirou Toura.

12:59.250 --> 13:05.130
The Sabaramond group imprisoned
 and murdered their human test subjects.

13:05.560 --> 13:11.470
And the two survivors started you guys, 
the Fire-Breathing Bug. Am I wrong?

13:14.640 --> 13:17.930
I have no idea what you're talking about.

13:18.280 --> 13:21.690
Unless you have a warrant,
 I can't play along with this any longer.

13:21.690 --> 13:24.300
Okay, then. Just tell me one more thing.

13:24.300 --> 13:28.660
One of our doctors took a look 
at those papers, and he said...

13:28.660 --> 13:34.230
This must be an experiment to implant 
abnormal principles in people.

13:34.230 --> 13:35.620
Fascinating.

13:35.970 --> 13:42.250
It combines special voices and sound waves 
to drill compressed data into the brain.

13:42.250 --> 13:46.260
Modern science doesn't approach 
human experimentation this way.

13:46.260 --> 13:49.740
So, the Fire-Breathing Bug inside all of you

13:49.740 --> 13:52.930
is a pseudo-personality 
implanted using hypnosis.

13:53.570 --> 13:56.360
The first Fire-Breathing Bugs are dead now,

13:56.360 --> 14:00.500
but they used that trick to 
multiply their will in this world.

14:00.500 --> 14:01.520
Isn't that right?

14:04.090 --> 14:05.710
I see.

14:05.710 --> 14:08.990
So, someone has arrived at the truth.

14:09.320 --> 14:11.570
I didn't do it alone.

14:11.570 --> 14:16.510
My predecessors laid the groundwork 
chasing all kinds of cases.

14:16.510 --> 14:19.710
Although that must come 
off as ironic to you guys.

14:19.920 --> 14:25.640
Never mind. You are righteous human beings.

14:25.640 --> 14:30.180
But how will you prove our crimes?

14:30.180 --> 14:36.730
All the arson you've committed would 
be tough to explain or prosecute.

14:36.730 --> 14:40.150
Then, why come here?

14:40.150 --> 14:46.610
Even if I can't arrest you, I figure 
I can stop you from striking again.

14:46.610 --> 14:49.490
Aiding and abetting a crime.

14:49.490 --> 14:51.820
You work with him, right?

14:52.170 --> 14:56.410
We're currently on the Solitaire task force.

14:56.410 --> 14:58.870
Now, I insist you show me!

14:59.170 --> 15:01.830
Show the moment this world flips over!

15:08.980 --> 15:10.180
What's wrong?

15:10.500 --> 15:12.640
Something made a big crash somewhere.

15:13.530 --> 15:15.210
I'll run ahead! Lulu!

15:15.210 --> 15:16.350
R-Right!

15:20.140 --> 15:23.560
<i>His sorcery is primitive. 
He's just firing mana.</i>

15:23.560 --> 15:25.480
<i>It makes no sense, even if he's holding back.</i>

15:25.930 --> 15:30.070
<i>He enhances his body well, but he 
casts other spells like an amateur!</i>

15:30.380 --> 15:33.990
A necromancer! You're the 
luckiest find I could hope for,

15:34.290 --> 15:37.520
but you refuse to become my friend!

15:37.520 --> 15:40.610
And you say you want "peace"?!

15:40.610 --> 15:42.650
With all your power?!

15:42.650 --> 15:43.960
That's a bad joke!

15:44.170 --> 15:48.360
You may be right, but I won't stop.

15:48.920 --> 15:52.130
My brother and my friends live in this world.

15:52.130 --> 15:53.890
I won't let you stand in 
the way of peace here.

15:56.970 --> 15:58.790
Fortune teller brat!

15:58.790 --> 16:00.430
You've gone and done it now!

16:01.280 --> 16:02.780
Looks like

16:02.780 --> 16:04.310
I'd better get seri—

16:08.810 --> 16:09.820
Good idea.

16:10.250 --> 16:13.910
I think you'd better give your 
all against <i>that one</i>, too.

16:13.910 --> 16:15.530
Gimme a break.

16:15.530 --> 16:18.080
Another brat?

16:20.180 --> 16:21.450
Civil-sama?!

16:21.850 --> 16:25.320
Great spirit! 
Please, grant Civil-sama your protection!

16:25.650 --> 16:27.020
Please, I beg you!

16:28.490 --> 16:30.340
A warning from the great spirit?

16:30.340 --> 16:33.170
And... I've never felt one so strong before.

16:38.180 --> 16:39.700
Found you!

16:40.190 --> 16:41.220
Polka-kun

16:42.010 --> 16:43.480
is coming back with me!

16:43.480 --> 16:44.400
Huh?

16:45.190 --> 16:48.770
Ah, yes. Truly magnificent!

16:49.090 --> 16:50.460
I'm so glad it was you!

16:50.460 --> 16:52.110
I'm only glad because it was you!

16:52.930 --> 16:55.920
A mere sorcerer could never change the world!

16:56.280 --> 17:00.490
You, however, can revolutionize 
this world all on your own.

17:00.490 --> 17:04.950
Your necromancy does nothing less 
than prove the existence of the soul!

17:04.950 --> 17:10.440
How many powerful people do you think 
crave eternal selfhood, even as a zombie?

17:10.440 --> 17:12.340
Make contracts with them,

17:12.340 --> 17:18.430
and you could even paint over this 
boring world with brand new values!

17:18.430 --> 17:21.110
And even if you don't want that,

17:21.110 --> 17:26.850
with our powers combined, you and I could 
bore a hole to the other side of the sky!

17:27.160 --> 17:28.580
We could go home!

17:28.580 --> 17:32.570
Leave this dull world for 
one where we truly belong!

17:34.670 --> 17:37.240
Whether you want it or not,

17:37.520 --> 17:42.200
if you won't change the world, 
we have no place here.

17:42.200 --> 17:43.160
Huh?

17:43.520 --> 17:45.460
<i>I don't believe it!</i>

17:45.460 --> 17:48.580
<i>His spells are starting to take proper shape!</i>

17:48.580 --> 17:52.050
Thank you for dazzling me with 
so many displays of your power.

17:52.730 --> 17:55.260
With your help, I'm slowly getting a handle

17:55.710 --> 17:58.620
on how to use magic.

17:59.450 --> 18:03.340
<i>He was definitely an amateur 
until a moment ago.</i>

18:03.340 --> 18:05.560
<i>He got this far just by seeing my spells?</i>

18:06.610 --> 18:07.520
<i>He's brilliant.</i>

18:07.870 --> 18:14.320
Now, let's fire a salute 
to celebrate our meeting.

18:18.620 --> 18:23.940
I knew you'd use fire, 
just like 100 years ago,

18:20.340 --> 18:24.410
<b><i>Fire
Safety</i></b>

18:25.900 --> 18:28.370
Sabaramond.

18:36.320 --> 18:41.510
So, this is the world you 
sorcerers saw on the other side!

18:44.450 --> 18:46.930
Elemental sorcery without elementals.

18:47.720 --> 18:50.380
That power doesn't exist in this world.

18:50.380 --> 18:51.900
No, it doesn't!

18:52.180 --> 18:55.150
Freaks with power like 
this shouldn't be here!

18:55.730 --> 18:58.740
You and I should either return to that world,

18:59.050 --> 19:01.200
or transform this one.

19:02.040 --> 19:04.910
Now, let's flip the world over.

19:04.910 --> 19:09.370
You've done it once before, 
haven't you, Corpse God?

19:09.760 --> 19:12.510
Or perhaps I should call you

19:12.510 --> 19:16.310
Rizdilusia Redrazalf, the Emperor Slayer?

19:16.310 --> 19:18.380
So, you know that much.

19:18.720 --> 19:23.000
I've read and reread reports on 
the Byandy Empire's major players.

19:23.500 --> 19:26.350
My heart leaped and burned with longing

19:27.120 --> 19:32.800
for the fairy tale world I couldn't 
touch, even though it birthed me.

19:33.310 --> 19:37.280
Now, show me more! More power 
from the other side of the sky!

19:40.140 --> 19:44.010
<i>She's gradually adjusting 
to my speed and movements.</i>

19:44.010 --> 19:45.740
<i>My right arm is my ace in the hole.</i>

19:45.740 --> 19:47.600
<i>If I don't finish her off 
with my first strike,</i>

19:47.600 --> 19:49.250
<i>she'll probably counter it.</i>

19:50.680 --> 19:53.630
<i>How does this guy know how I move?</i>

19:54.180 --> 19:57.840
<i>I never thought training with those 
tigers would pay off like this.</i>

19:57.840 --> 19:59.980
<i>They breathe similarly when they attack.</i>

19:59.980 --> 20:02.300
<i>No, make that "almost identically."</i>

20:02.590 --> 20:05.400
<i>She's a savage beast in human form.</i>

20:05.400 --> 20:08.510
<i>And that's why I have a better 
shot against her than the tigers!</i>

20:08.820 --> 20:11.350
<i>She's doesn't defy reason.</i>

20:11.350 --> 20:14.560
<i>That's reserved for people 
like Majiri Agakura</i>

20:14.560 --> 20:15.770
<i>and Lemmi—</i>

20:20.510 --> 20:22.330
Great spirit, why?!

20:24.370 --> 20:27.320
Is this what that "elemental" can do?

20:27.670 --> 20:31.370
Wow! It's got no, like... How do I put this?

20:31.370 --> 20:33.790
You know how hostility and 
stuff signals attacks?

20:33.790 --> 20:35.640
I couldn't sense any of that!

20:35.640 --> 20:36.880
E-Excuse me?

20:36.880 --> 20:40.600
Oh, I'm Misaki. Nice meeting you!

20:40.600 --> 20:44.840
I know this is sudden, but would you 
give me back that shark plushie?

20:44.930 --> 20:45.300
Squeeze

20:45.450 --> 20:47.080
I can't do that!

20:47.080 --> 20:50.810
Guarding this is my assigned duty!

20:52.090 --> 20:53.270
That figures.

20:53.270 --> 20:54.860
Okay, I get it.

20:54.860 --> 20:56.930
So, unless I slip past this thing,

20:56.930 --> 21:00.480
I can't rescue the real Polka-kun.

21:00.740 --> 21:01.970
Oh, damn it!

21:01.970 --> 21:03.700
How's he gonna get this under control?!

21:04.020 --> 21:06.940
Can you seriously handle this, Polka?

21:06.940 --> 21:08.630
You're right.

21:08.630 --> 21:09.400
Huh?

21:09.850 --> 21:14.400
In the end, both you and 
I clash with this world.

21:15.290 --> 21:18.380
And my presence as a stranger to this world

21:18.630 --> 21:21.590
attracted an elemental 
that could level this city

21:21.900 --> 21:26.550
and you, a wielder of otherworldly powers.

21:27.520 --> 21:31.950
So I'll put a stop to you here and 
return this body to Polka-kun.

21:31.950 --> 21:35.020
Then, if I go off somewhere and disappear,

21:35.020 --> 21:36.940
this city will know peace.

21:37.600 --> 21:42.530
I don't know how the documents 
you read described me,

21:43.130 --> 21:45.330
but this is no fairy tale.

21:45.750 --> 21:48.250
Regret that you opposed me.

21:49.650 --> 21:54.500
My name and rank perished with my country.

21:55.840 --> 21:59.290
Only a soul that failed to die remains.

21:59.690 --> 22:02.730
I am accustomed to playing the world's foe.
